{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/331297-npc-character-ideas-let-s-post-some","id":331297,"title":"NPC Character Ideas, let's post some :)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-12-05T10:55:51-08:00","id":331297,"title":"NPC Character Ideas, let's post some :)","content":"Sometimes it is a bugger to design or get ideas for new NPC's, and for some it is always an nightmare. Then for other one can snap out ten in a row in the moment as needed. But having a repository of ideas is always useful. Let's post some ideas up, but:<br /> <br /> - no stats.<br /> - only a few lines and a name. <br /> - do not place the npc in a special city and if at a locale make it location neutral<br /> <br /> ---------<br /> <br /> <u><b>Teary-Eyed Mary</b></u><br /> <br /> Nobody really knows her story, but she sits at the pier at every sunset and sundown. Eyes swelling, but instead of tears, black streaks of ink roll down her cheek. Giving her a harrowed appearance. But as soon as the sundown/sunset is over the black streaks vanishes as black mist and she stops crying. And it is if nothing ever had happened. What is her story, what did happen here and why does her tears become like ink?<br /> <br /> <u><b>Side-Stepping Lars</b></u><br /> <br /> In the second side street to the east from the town centre there is a shadowy person. He have never been seen outside his street. but many say they see him leave it is like he disappears. He walks out sideways and vanishes. nobody now who he is and why he does it. some say he walks into the tempest - others say he is something worse, a spectre that culls the dead like an invisible horror.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1159-kjetilkverndokken","name":"kjetilkverndokken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1159_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-05T13:55:19-08:00","id":331453,"title":"","content":"This got a bit longer than I had hoped, but I simply couldn't cut it down anymore. It's a shortened version of a longer concept I wrote <a href=\"http://www.shadownesssence.com/forum/index.php?/topic/9286-character-concepts/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> ages ago.<br /> <br /> <b>The Clockwork Man</b><br /> <br /> He was called Jeremy, though his real name was Jeremiah. The kids called him the Clockwork Man, because all he ever did was sit in his workshop and work on his clocks. <br /> When Jeremy was young, his father was the clock maker. A brutal man, given to drinking and spontaneous outbursts of rage directed at Jeremy or his mother. Not a happy childhood, by any standards.But Jeremy had a dream. unconquered by his violent father, Jeremy dreamt stories. He dreamt of pageants and plays, fables and fairytales, and he took comfort in their wonder and excitement. He took up his fathers trade, and slowly the dreams faded away. He became absorbed with his fathers clocks, and never went out when he was not at work. When his father died, he did not even have the energy to smile.And one day, many years after, he simply did not get out of bed. <br /> And then he died.<br /> The children had gotten it right. They had called him the Clockwork Man, and they had shuddered when they passed his shop, never knowing how right they were. The final decades of his life Jeremy had spent as if propelled by clockwork. He had felt like a Clockwork Man, as if giant cogweels and coiled springs was all that filled him, all that made him continue his mundane, soul-killing work for year after year.<br /> Now, beyond the Shroud, he truly was a Clockwork man. His Corpus reflected the death of his dreams, and now his torso was open at the front and filled with bizarre clockwork, giant cogweels and coiled springs. Wherever he walked a ticking followed him, the meticulous scream of his dying soul.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4449-eisenkreutzer","name":"EisenKreutzer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4449_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}